#: src/reference/changes/migrating-from-sbt-1.x.md:111
msgid "Changes to `%%`"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/changes/migrating-from-sbt-1.x.md:114
msgid ""
"In sbt 2.x, `ModuleID`'s `%%` operator has become platform-aware. For JVM "
"subprojects, `%%` works as before, encoding Scala suffix (for example `_3`) "
"on Maven repositories."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/changes/migrating-from-sbt-1.x.md:116
msgid "Migrating `%%%` operator"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/changes/migrating-from-sbt-1.x.md:118
msgid ""
"When Scala.JS or Scala Native becomes available on sbt 2.x, `%%` will encode "
"both the Scala version (such as `_3`) and the platform suffix (`_sjs1` etc). "
"As a result, `%%%` can be replaced with `%%`:"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/changes/migrating-from-sbt-1.x.md:121
msgid "\"org.scala-js\""
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/changes/migrating-from-sbt-1.x.md:121
msgid "\"scalajs-dom\""
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/changes/migrating-from-sbt-1.x.md:121
msgid "\"2.8.0\""
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/changes/migrating-from-sbt-1.x.md:124
msgid "Use `.platform(Platform.jvm)` in case where JVM libraries are needed."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/changes/migrating-from-sbt-1.x.md:126
msgid "Changes to `target`"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/changes/migrating-from-sbt-1.x.md:129
msgid ""
"In sbt 2.x, the `target` directory is unified to be a single `target/` "
"directory in the working directory, and each subproject creates a "
"subdirectory encoding platform, Scala version, and the subproject id. To "
"absorb this change in scripted tests, `exists`, `absent`, and `delete` now "
"supports glob expression `**`, as well as `||`."
msgstr ""

